# Global absorb ceiling of 75 percent per combat type (server/README.md "Absorb ceiling"). Owner decision 2026-10-20.
# Before: equipment absorbs (Player::blockHit, item abilities, each one applied to what was left) and the absorb storages
# (rarity_onCombat_absorbs.lua, after blockHit: gear rarity storages 977544-977553/972/974 plus the passive tree and Paragon
# storages 977562-977575, summed, no cap) stacked without limit and could pass 100 percent on one element.
# After: in Player::blockHit the equipment part is raised back so that (equipment and storages) together never remove more
# than CHAOS_ABSORB_CEILING_PERCENT (75, player.cpp, the one place to change). The storage part is read with
# Player::getStorageValue, so equipment takes at most 25/(100-storage) of the hit; with storages at 75 or more, equipment
# takes nothing more. Not covered: the Lua event itself still takes the full storage sum after blockHit, so the storage
# sum must stay at or under 75 (passivetree_effects.lua maxAbsorb 75, see README) or the ceiling is only met for equipment.
# Applies after 0001-0048: patch -p1 < 0049-absorb-ceiling.patch, then rebuild (applies cleanly; NOT compiled).
